  <keywords>
    <keyword>folder</keyword>
    <keyword>icon</keyword>
    <keyword>customize</keyword>
    <keyword>pictogram</keyword>
    <keyword>emoji</keyword>
    <keyword>color</keyword>
    <keyword>Nautilus</keyword>
    <keyword>Dolphin</keyword>
  </keywords>

  <branding>
    <color type="primary" scheme_preference="light">#a8d8e6</color>
    <color type="primary" scheme_preference="dark">#14758f</color>
  </branding>

  <developer id="io.github.gor3pig">
    <name translate="no">Gor3pig</name>
  </developer>

  <launchable type="desktop-id">io.github.gor3pig.Custicon.desktop</launchable>
  <provides>
    <binary>custicon</binary>
  </provides>

  <url type="homepage">https://gor3pig.github.io/Custicon/</url>
  <url type="vcs-browser">https://github.com/Gor3pig/Custicon</url>
  <url type="bugtracker">https://github.com/Gor3pig/Custicon/issues</url>
  <url type="help">https://github.com/Gor3pig/Custicon/blob/main/help/en/README.md</url>
  <url type="contribute">https://github.com/Gor3pig/Custicon/blob/main/docs/development.md</url>

  <requires>
    <display_length compare="ge">360</display_length>
  </requires>
  <supports>
    <control>keyboard</control>
    <control>pointing</control>
    <control>touch</control>
  </supports>

  <content_rating type="oars-1.1"/>

  <releases>
    <release version="1.8.2" date="2026-11-17">
      <description>
        <p>The custom color picker is easier to use.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>A larger plane to choose a color freely: dragging keeps working when the pointer leaves the area, and a long press no longer interrupts it</li>
          <li>A hue bar, a hexadecimal code field, and the previous color shown next to the new one</li>
          <li>The arrow keys move the choice, and Shift makes bigger steps</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.8.1" date="2026-11-16">
      <description>
        <p>The value fields next to the sliders are simpler.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>The field next to each slider no longer has plus and minus buttons: type a value, then press Enter or leave the field</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.8.0" date="2026-11-16">
      <description>
        <p>A light, dark or system theme, typed values for the sliders, a clearer menu, and an editor that adapts to the window.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Choose System, Light or Dark with three round swatches at the top of the main menu: the choice is kept from one launch to the next</li>
          <li>Type a value in the field next to each slider: size, position and badge size</li>
          <li>The main menu is organized in sections: icons, icon sets, styles and backup</li>
          <li>The custom icon sets dialog is larger</li>
          <li>The editor adapts to narrow and wide windows: the buttons at the bottom wrap instead of overflowing, and the preview is drawn larger when there is room</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.7.0" date="2026-11-15">
      <description>
        <p>Your own icon sets, a repair dialog, and icons on symbolic links.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Add a folder of SVG files as a set of your own, then add or remove icons one by one: it appears in the picker and keeps working even if you remove the set</li>
          <li>A bar tells you how many folders need a check, and one dialog repairs them, only the way you choose</li>
          <li>A symbolic link to a folder, on your desktop for example, can have its own icon with GNOME, Cinnamon and MATE</li>
          <li>Safer handling of damaged data and of unusual text in saved settings</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.6.0" date="2026-11-15">
      <description>
        <p>A corner badge can now be put alone on a folder, and the texts speak of your desktop environment.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Remove the central pictogram to keep only the corner badge on the folder icon</li>
          <li>The About dialog, the store entry and the website now name the desktop environments instead of one file manager</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.5.0" date="2026-11-15">
      <description>
        <p>Custicon now works with KDE Plasma and other desktops, and can remove several icons at once.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>KDE Plasma (Dolphin) and LXQt (PCManFM-Qt) are supported, in addition to GNOME, Cinnamon and MATE: the right method is chosen automatically</li>
          <li>With Dolphin and PCManFM-Qt the icon is kept in a small hidden .directory file inside the folder, which is removed when you remove the icon</li>
          <li>A banner tells you when your file manager (Thunar, PCManFM, COSMIC Files) cannot show custom folder icons</li>
          <li>Remove the icons of several folders in one step, with a confirmation and an Undo for the whole batch</li>
          <li>The texts now speak of your file manager instead of Nautilus only</li>
          <li>A corner badge: a small colored disc with its own pictogram next to the central one</li>
          <li>Save all your settings in one file and restore them later</li>
          <li>A complete page in the app store, with screenshots, keywords and categories for every desktop</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.4.2" date="2026-11-15">
      <description>
        <p>Custicon now works on openSUSE Tumbleweed without changing its permissions.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Access to the home folder is now read and write: the read-only form did not work on every system, and Custicon had to be allowed more access by hand</li>
          <li>Custicon still never writes in your folders: the icon is saved by the GVfs service of your session</li>
          <li>The custom color is now a round rainbow swatch that shows the chosen color in its center</li>
          <li>The help and the documentation describe the permissions as they really are</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.4.1" date="2026-11-14">
      <description>
        <p>A faster interface, readable in dark mode, and a window that remembers its size.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Custicon now asks for GPU acceleration by default, so the interface is drawn by your graphics card</li>
          <li>The bundled pictograms (Phosphor, emoji, logos) follow the text color and are readable in the dark style</li>
          <li>The folder list and the picker are lighter: regaining focus and switching sets are quicker</li>
          <li>The main preview is smaller, and the window opens at a size that shows everything, then remembers its size and whether it was maximized</li>
          <li>The help explains how to restore a permission with Flatseal or for an installation for all users</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.4.0" date="2026-11-14">
      <description>
        <p>Many more pictograms, a roomier editor and several folders at once.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>The whole Phosphor set (1,500 pictograms), plus about 1,600 monochrome emoji and 3,400 brand logos, found by name in English or French</li>
          <li>Suggestions that follow the name of the folder, and your recent and favorite pictograms</li>
          <li>A new editor in two columns that needs no scrolling: choose colors from a palette, drag the pictogram on the preview and scroll to resize it</li>
          <li>Customize several folders at once, from the folder chooser, by dropping them, or by ticking them in the list</li>
          <li>The README is simpler, and the website now has a slideshow and follows the language of your browser</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.3.0" date="2026-11-14">
      <description>
        <p>More pictograms, a tinted folder and a complete About dialog.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Choose a pictogram from the new Phosphor set, bundled with Custicon, as well as from your icon theme</li>
          <li>Tint the folder itself: no tint, the accent color of your system, or a color of your own</li>
          <li>The automatic color of the pictogram follows the tinted folder</li>
          <li>A complete About dialog with the release notes, and a Help entry (F1) that opens the guide in your language</li>
          <li>Custicon detects more reliably when access to the home folder is missing</li>
          <li>The README and the user guide are available in English and French</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.2.0" date="2026-11-13">
      <description>
        <p>New ways to customize and to manage folders.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Choose the color of the pictogram: automatic, the accent color of your system, or your own</li>
          <li>Use letters or symbols as a pictogram</li>
          <li>Save the appearance as named styles, and export or import them</li>
          <li>The appearance you applied is proposed again for the next folders you add, and can still be changed</li>
          <li>Open a folder in Custicon from Nautilus, with a drag and drop, or from the command line</li>
          <li>Search pictograms in French, and search your customized folders</li>
          <li>Find a folder that was moved or renamed, undo a removal, and remove all icons at once</li>
          <li>A banner offers to regenerate the icons when the icon theme or the accent color changed</li>
          <li>Finer sliders and a more compact list of folders</li>
          <li>Custicon explains how to allow access to the home folder when it is missing</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="1.0.0" date="2026-11-13">
      <description>
        <p>The first stable version of Custicon.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Put a pictogram on the real folder icon of your current icon theme</li>
          <li>Choose a pictogram from your icon theme, or use your own SVG or PNG file</li>
          <li>Let the color be chosen automatically, or set the color, the size and the position yourself</li>
          <li>See the result live before applying it</li>
          <li>Remove an icon at any time: the folder gets back the icon it had before</li>
          <li>Regenerate every icon after a change of icon theme</li>
          <li>The content of your folders is never modified</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
  </releases>
</component>
